  "kind": "per-socket pipeline experiment (not a milestone)",
  "date": "2026-11-22",
  "question": "Does running diagsteno ingest as one complete pipeline per socket (stagelanes pinning and rings, socket-local memory) beat diagsteno's single unpinned ingest on the Dell?",
  "machine": {
    "name": "dell",
    "host": "Dell PowerEdge R440, 2x Intel Xeon Silver 4214 (12 cores each, HT on), Proxmox VE 9.2.21 (kernel 7.0.14-25-pve); VM 102 the only guest running",
    "host_memory_per_node": "node 0: 3x 32 GB DDR4-2400; node 1: 2x 32 GB DDR4-2400",
    "guest": "KVM VM 102, cpu=host, 24 vCPUs (2 sockets x 12 cores), 2 NUMA nodes",
    "pinning": "hookscript pin-102.sh: vCPU 0-11 -> host CPUs 0,2,...,22 (node 0), 12-23 -> 1,3,...,23 (node 1); numa0/numa1 policy=bind to host nodes 0/1; verified on the host 2026-11-22",
    "storage": "/dev/shm (tmpfs, memory-backed: fsync is a no-op) and ~/.cache (ext4 on LVM on a QEMU disk on a ZFS pool of 4x WD Blue SA510 SATA SSDs without power-loss protection, behind a PERC H730P)"
  },
  "os": "Ubuntu 26.04.1 LTS",
  "kernel": "7.0.0-43-generic",
  "rust": "rustc 1.95.0 (59807616e 2026-04-14), release profile",
  "gpu": "none",
  "gpu_driver": "n/a",
  "wgpu_backend": "n/a",
  "gpu_host_link": "n/a",
  "network": "loopback (127.0.0.1), sender and ingest on the same guest",
  "commits": {
    "paralanes": "exp-per-socket-pipeline, experiments/per-socket-pipeline (code at 67ea9f6 before an amend that only removed build output)",
    "diagsteno": "f6d1014 (main, M7 merged)",
    "stagelanes": "b09f58f (main)",
    "bytelanes": "main with M7 FFT"
  },
  "commands": [
    "cd paralanes/experiments/per-socket-pipeline && cargo build --release",
    "for r in 1 2 3; do for store in /dev/shm/psp ~/.cache/psp-disk; do for l in baseline per-socket per-socket-unpinned; do ./target/release/per-socket-pipeline --layout $l --store-dir $store --seconds 60; done; done; done"
  ],
  "workload": "60 s of the default 64-channel synthetic layout (seed 2026): 384,000 frames, 51,072,000 samples, 13,856 feature windows; sent unpaced (as fast as ingest accepts) over TCP; every batch stored durably (Parquet + fsync) before it is acknowledged",
  "layouts": {
    "baseline": "diagsteno::ingest::Ingest: reader thread, writer thread (store + ack), ONE feature thread; unpinned; one sender with all 64 channels",
    "per-socket": "2 shards, shard s = accel 16s..16s+15 and strain 32+16s..32+16s+15, all threads pinned to socket s: ingest core, store core, 4 feature cores, sender core; stagelanes-ring SPSC rings between stages; own TCP port and store directory per shard",
    "per-socket-unpinned": "the same 2 shards with no pinning"
  },
  "fairness_note": "The baseline has 1 feature thread and 1 store thread; per-socket layouts have 8 feature threads and 2 store threads. Differences between baseline and per-socket therefore mix parallelism with placement. Pinned vs unpinned per-socket isolates placement.",
